# 12碼讀心戰 (Penalty Mind Game v2) - Round 3 Fix Report

**Date**: 2026-10-24
**Status**: COMPLETE (ALL CRITICAL, MAJOR & SENSIBLE MINORS RESOLVED)
**Test Suite**: 10 Unit & Integration Suites (75/75 tests passing, 100% green)
**Browser E2E Verification**: Real Headless Chrome 390×844 CDP verification (100% green, 0 console errors)

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Verification Highlights

Following the code review in `reviews/grok-v2-r3.md`, all CRITICAL, MAJOR, and sensible MINOR issues have been addressed and verified:

1. **單場快速對決 Swipe Shooting Fully Restored**:
   - Resolved the pointer event blocking issue where the first-run tutorial overlay (`.tutorial-overlay`, `.ghost-hand-track`, `.tutorial-prompt-box`) intercepted mouse and touch gestures over the ball.
   - Configured `#screen-match * { pointer-events: none !important; }` and `.tutorial-overlay, .tutorial-overlay * { pointer-events: none !important; }`, re-enabling pointer interaction strictly on actual interactive buttons (`button`, `.btn-skip-replay`, `[role="button"]`, `.icon-btn`).
   - Added `#screen-match { overflow: hidden !important; }` to eliminate full-screen match HUD scrollport behavior.
   - **Headless CDP Verification**: Executed real pointer swipe from `(195, 780)` to `(195, 500)` on a fresh profile (`totalShots = 0`, tutorial prompt active). Verified ball physics simulation fired immediately, recorded the kick, and resolved cleanly without obstruction.

2. **「世界盃淘汰賽 (16隊爭霸)」 CTA & Bracket Transition**:
   - Removed inline `style="display: none;"` from `<div id="modal-team-select">` in `index.html` which previously prevented `.active` (`display: flex`) from showing the team picker.
   - Aligned `openTournamentScreen()` and `btnConfirmTeam` in `src/main.js` so clicking the title CTA opens the modal, confirms team selection, renders the 8-match R16 bracket, and transitions directly to `#screen-tournament`.
   - Cancel fallback cleanly navigates home if a tournament is not active.

3. **Stars Meta Loop & End Screen Field Alignment**:
   - In `src/unlocks.js`, supported parameter aliasing across naming conventions: `won`/`isWin`, `isTournament`/`isTournamentMatch`, `isChampion`/`isTournamentFinalWin`, `predictability`/`predictabilityScore`.
   - Updated breakdown item objects to supply both `{ label, count, desc: label, stars: count }` so end-screen template strings render `${item.label}` and `+${item.count} ⭐` cleanly without `undefined+undefined`.
   - Added unit test in `tests/unlocks.test.js` validating the live payload.

4. **Crowd Rendering & Animation Performance**:
   - Replaced `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial` on crowd torso and head instanced meshes with lightweight `THREE.MeshBasicMaterial`.
   - Replaced 20 individual terrace step meshes with 2 `THREE.InstancedMesh` instances (step risers and edge trims), saving 18 draw calls.
   - Eliminated per-frame `new THREE.Object3D()` and matrix decomposes in `stadium.update()` by writing directly to `instanceMatrix.array[i * 16 + 13]`.
   - Added check to skip crowd bobbing when `document.hidden` or `prefersReducedMotion` is active.

5. **Housekeeping & Documentation**:
   - Removed legacy v1 2D prototype archive from `CHANGELOG.md` and appended `## v2 Round 3 fixes`.
   - Updated `ASSETS.md` to reference `vendor/three.module.min.js`.
   - Silenced noisy `console.warn` on intentional corrupt JSON test fixtures in `src/tournament.js` and `src/unlocks.js`.
   - Re-captured all 8 reference screenshots at 390×844 resolution in `screenshots/r3-390/`.

