## 2. Detailed Issue Resolutions

### CRITICAL 1: Pointer Events HUD Blocking on Match Screen (`style.css`, `index.html`, `src/input.js`)
- **Problem**: On a fresh profile (`totalShots < 2`), `.tutorial-overlay` was displayed. Because `#screen-match` (`z-index: 20`) sat above canvas `#scene` (`z-index: 1`), and CSS `pointer-events: none` is not inherited by child elements with default styles, the tutorial prompt box and ghost hand intercepted pointer hits at `y=780` and `y=650`. As a result, `onPointerDown` never triggered on the canvas and shots could not be launched.
- **Fix**:
  - In `style.css`:
    ```css
    #screen-match {
      overflow: hidden !important;
      pointer-events: none !important;
    }
    #screen-match * {
      pointer-events: none !important;
    }
    #screen-match button,
    #screen-match .btn-skip-replay,
    #screen-match [role="button"],
    #screen-match .icon-btn {
      pointer-events: auto !important;
    }
    .tutorial-overlay,
    .tutorial-overlay * {
      pointer-events: none !important;
    }
    ```
  - In `index.html`: Added inline `pointer-events: none;` on `#tutorial-overlay` and children.
- **Verification**: Verified via `document.elementFromPoint(195, 780)` returning `<canvas id="scene">`. Real CDP mouse drag from `(195, 780)` to `(195, 500)` fires the shot and increments `totalShots` to 1.

### CRITICAL 2: World Cup Title CTA & Bracket Navigation (`index.html`, `src/main.js`)
- **Problem**: In `index.html`, `#modal-team-select` had an inline `style="display: none;"`. Adding `.active` (`display: flex`) failed to override the inline style due to CSS specificity. Furthermore, `openTournamentScreen()` returned early on fresh saves without switching screen to `'tournament'`.
- **Fix**:
  - Removed `style="display: none;"` from `#modal-team-select` in `index.html`.
  - In `src/main.js`:
    - In `openTournamentScreen()`: switches to `'tournament'` immediately, and opens the team modal if tournament is not active.
    - In `openTeamSelectModal()`: sets `this.dom.modalTeamSelect.style.display = 'flex'`.
    - In `btnConfirmTeam`: starts tournament with chosen team, hides modal, renders bracket, and switches to `'tournament'`.
    - In `btnCancelTeam`: if tournament is not active, cleanly navigates home via `goHome()`.
- **Verification**: Title CTA opens team select, selecting Hong Kong confirms and transitions to `#screen-tournament`, rendering all 8 R16 bracket matches.

### MAJOR 3: Stars Meta Loop & End Screen Field Alignment (`src/unlocks.js`, `src/main.js`, `tests/unlocks.test.js`)
- **Problem**: `calculateMatchStars` expected `{ won, isTournament, isChampion, predictability }` but `finishMatch` passed `{ isWin, isTournamentMatch, isTournamentFinalWin, predictabilityScore }`. Additionally, end-screen template strings rendered `${item.label}` and `+${item.count} ⭐` while `calculateMatchStars` emitted `{ desc, stars }`, producing `undefined+undefined ⭐`.
- **Fix**:
  - In `src/unlocks.js`, accepted both naming variants:
    ```javascript
    const won = !!(stats.won ?? stats.isWin);
    const isTournament = !!(stats.isTournament ?? stats.isTournamentMatch);
    const isChampion = !!(stats.isChampion ?? stats.isTournamentFinalWin);
    const predictability = stats.predictability ?? stats.predictabilityScore ?? null;
    ```
  - Emitted dual-aliased breakdown objects:
    ```javascript
    breakdown.push({ label, count, desc: label, stars: count });
    ```
  - In `src/main.js:1871-1872`:
    ```javascript
    const label = item.label || item.desc || '獎勵';
    const count = item.count ?? item.stars ?? 1;
    ```
  - Added unit test in `tests/unlocks.test.js` validating the exact structure emitted by `finishMatch`.
- **Verification**: `07_screen_end_stars.png` displays clean star breakdown rows without `undefined`.

### MAJOR 4: Crowd Rendering & Animation Performance (`src/scene.js`)
- **Problem**: Stadium crowd used 2x260 standard lit meshes, allocating two `THREE.Object3D()` instances and performing 520 `decompose` + `setMatrixAt` calls every frame, causing SwiftShader CPU rendering drops. Terrace steps were also 20 separate uninstanced box meshes.
- **Fix**:
  - Converted crowd torso and head instanced meshes to `THREE.MeshBasicMaterial`.
  - Instanced the 10 terrace steps and 10 edge trims into 2 `THREE.InstancedMesh` instances (saving 18 draw calls).
  - Hoisted dummy `Object3D`s and updated spectator bobbing in `stadium.update()` by writing directly to `instanceMatrix.array[i * 16 + 13]`:
    ```javascript
    const tArr = this.crowdTorsoMesh.instanceMatrix.array;
    const hArr = this.crowdHeadMesh.instanceMatrix.array;
    for (let i = 0; i < this.crowdCount; i++) {
      const dy = Math.sin(time * 3.0 + (i % 7) * 0.9) * 0.035;
      tArr[i * 16 + 13] = this.crowdBaseY[i] + dy;
      hArr[i * 16 + 13] = this.crowdBaseY[i] + 0.30 + dy;
    }
    this.crowdTorsoMesh.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;
    this.crowdHeadMesh.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;
    ```
  - Added check to skip bobbing when `document.hidden` or `prefersReducedMotion` is active.
- **Verification**: Crowd renders at unlit basic shader cost with 0 per-frame object allocations.

### MAJOR 5: Match Screen Overflow (`style.css`)
- **Problem**: Global `.screen { overflow-y: auto }` turned the transparent match HUD into a scrollable container.
- **Fix**: Set `#screen-match { overflow: hidden !important; }`, keeping `overflow-y: auto` only for `#screen-tournament, #screen-locker, #screen-title, #screen-end`.
- **Verification**: Match screen HUD remains fixed and non-scrollable.

### MINOR 6: Clean v1 Archive in `CHANGELOG.md`
- Removed legacy 2D prototype sections from `CHANGELOG.md` and appended `## v2 Round 3 fixes`.

### MINOR 7: Fix `ASSETS.md` Three.js Reference
- Updated path in `ASSETS.md` to `vendor/three.module.min.js`.

### MINOR 8: Silence Storage Warnings on Corrupted JSON
- Silenced noisy `console.warn` during test corrupted JSON handling in `src/tournament.js` and `src/unlocks.js`.

